[gd_resource type="Environment" load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://cq2gubsafarienv"]

; Environment for Kopje Crossing. Noon on a high savanna, and the brightest
; thing in the game by some way — Rust is mid-afternoon in a container yard and
; `arena_env.tres` is the island's torch-lit dusk (D-009).
;
; Derived from `rust_env.tres`, and only the numbers that make midday different
; from afternoon were changed. That is deliberate: the two static maps should
; not need different eyes, so the tonemapping, the glow and the SSAO below are
; Rust's, unaltered, and the sky and the fog are the whole of the difference.
;
;   * A bluer, harder sky. `sky_top` goes from (0.26, 0.44, 0.74) to
;     (0.28, 0.50, 0.86) and the horizon from dusty to pale gold — the sun is
;     overhead rather than low, so there is less atmosphere between the camera
;     and the top of the sky and more of it at the rim.
;   * A *paler ground half*, at (0.78, 0.68, 0.50) into (0.45, 0.36, 0.25). The
;     sky's lower hemisphere is the only bounce light in the scene
;     (`ambient_light_source` is the sky), and on this map that bounce is coming
;     off sand. With Rust's darker ground colours the shaded side of every rock
;     went blue, which is the one thing that stops a savanna reading as hot.
;   * **`background_energy_multiplier` is the exposure control**, not
;     `ambient_light_energy` — see the long note in `rust_env.tres`, which
;     measured it. 1.35 rather than Rust's 1.45: this map is 96 m of pale sand
;     under a 64-degree sun and there is nothing here like the drilling tower's
;     shadow to lift.
;
; Measured, not guessed, the way Rust's 1.45 was. Rendered at 1000x1000 through
; `tools/parkour_report.tscn` (iso) and 1280x720 through `tools/preview_map.tscn`
; (pad0), then counted with PIL:
;
;     view    below 8/255    at 255 in all channels
;     iso        0.60 %            0.00 %
;     pad0       0.00 %            0.00 %
;
; against a budget of under 2 % crushed and under 1 % clipped. At
; background_energy 1.6 the pad0 view put 1.4 % of the frame at 255 — the sand
; in the middle distance blew out first, before anything in the sky did.
;
; Fog is thinner than Rust's (0.0009 against 0.0016) and sits lower: the map is
; 96 m across and the whole point of the outer band is that you can see someone
; walking in from a spawn pad forty metres away. The height fog at -3 with a
; density of 0.015 is doing the opposite job — it pools in the bottom of the
; cliff skirt so the edge of the world has some depth to it.

